# Prohibited Terminology and Patterns Rules

## Terminology Corrections
- Rule: Never use "DeltaOne token"
  - Correction: Use "Hokusai token" instead
  - Reason: Maintains consistent branding and terminology

- Rule: Never use "Company"
  - Correction: Use "protocol" instead
  - Reason: Accurately reflects the decentralized nature of the system

- Rule: Never state "All data gets tokens"
  - Correction: Clarify that tokens are only rewarded if performance improves
  - Reason: Ensures accurate representation of the reward mechanism

## Avoided Practices
- Rule: No overpromising rewards
  - Context: When discussing token rewards or incentives
  - Impact: Prevents misleading expectations

- Rule: No suggesting pre-minting
  - Context: When discussing token distribution or supply
  - Impact: Maintains protocol integrity

- Rule: No describing speculative token behavior
  - Context: When discussing token economics or value
  - Impact: Focuses on utility rather than speculation
